WEBVTT

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:08.300
Every action gives the world a new answer.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.500
Today's models see the frames but miss the changes.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:21.500
How does a baby learn space? By moving, using its hands, and interacting with the world.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:31.500
We use action to understand why the world changes.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.500
One interaction links observation, action, and new observation.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:49.500
Three stages: passive world change, active self-motion, and long-trajectory integration.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.500
108K verifiable interaction QA pairs.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:03.500
Two-stage training: SFT learns local transitions; OPD connects them into complete states.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:12.500
A 32-frame trajectory: how far did the camera move?

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.500
Local displacements form a 20-meter path; endpoints are 2 meters apart.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:22.000
What is the motion sequence of the complete trajectory?

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:31.500
Forward, left, forward, left, forward: five transitions form a complete state.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:38.500
One interaction becomes the next capability.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:45.408
Understand the world through interaction, and keep improving.
